  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## 4.0.0-build.41 (unreleased)\n\n- Add `SumDistinct`, `Ilike` with an optional escape character, and `RegexpInstr`\n  with an optional index. Keep the existing `Column.ILike` and\n  `RegexpExtractInstr` APIs available.\n- Fix `WindowFunction.Window` when a start offset is supplied without a slide\n  duration: the window duration is used as the slide duration and the offset is\n  passed in the correct argument position.\n- Add Spark 4.0 null helpers: `NullIfZero` (also available as `Nullifzero`) and\n  `Zeroifnull`.\n- Add Spark 4.0 UTF-8 functions: `IsValidUtf8`, `MakeValidUtf8`, `ValidateUtf8`,\n  and `TryValidateUtf8`.\n- Add Spark 4.0 string aggregation: `Listagg`, `ListaggDistinct`, `StringAgg`,\n  and `StringAggDistinct`, with string, binary, and expression delimiters.\n  Distinct variants use Spark Connect's distinct flag on the base aggregate.\n- Add plan and result tests for these functions, covering duplicates, nulls,\n  empty input, invalid UTF-8, and binary delimiters. Update the function-status table.\n- Include the latest release notes in both NuGet packages' release-note metadata.\n- Fix `Column.IsIn()` adding an unintended string literal when an argument is a\n  `Column`. Both the params and list overloads now preserve column arguments.\n- Add regression tests for column, literal, and mixed arguments.\n- Run the full test suite on Spark 4.0.0 with Delta Lake 4.0.0, and add a Spark 3.5.6\n  smoke-test job. Use archived Spark downloads and retain test results and server logs.\n- Give the local Spark and Databricks workflows separate concurrency groups.\n- Share the version of both NuGet packages and pack them in CI.\n- Refresh the local quickstart, compatibility documentation, and packaging instructions.\n\nThe .NET 8 target and existing Spark API baseline are unchanged.",
